messages.content:
Analyze the Jira bug report title and description and the seed changes that were made to fix the reported bug. Combine this analysis with the initial static impact set, which contains the fully qualified names of code entities that are statically related to the seed changes.
For each entity in the initial static impact set, analyze its relationship to the seed changes and collect evidence indicating whether the entity must be modified as a consequence of the seed changes.  Furthermore, identify any additional code entities that must be modified or created and collect supporting evidence.
Focus on production code, not test code or other files.
Inputs: - Jira bug report title: NPE in XmlReportOutputter - Jira bug report description: {code}
public void output(ConfigurationResolveReport report, String resolveId, String[] confs, ResolutionCacheManager cacheMgr) throws IOException {
 File reportFile = cacheMgr.getConfigurationResolveReportInCache(resolveId,
 report.getConfiguration());
 File reportParentDir = reportFile.getParentFile();
 reportParentDir.mkdirs(); // NPE
 OutputStream stream = new FileOutputStream(reportFile);
 writer.output(report, confs, stream);
 stream.close();
 //...
}
{code}
In XmlReportOutputter.output method, NPE occurs when reportFile.getParentFile() returns null. I think a proper error handling is needed for reportFile and reportParentDir before OutputStream is created.

